  "note": "Proportional representation (single transferable vote) under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1919; polled Saturday 5 June 1920 and counted at Armagh by T. E. Reid, secretary of the county council and returning officer. Armagh electoral area (three seats): the district electoral divisions of Armagh Rural, Charlemont, Grange, Kilmore, Loughgall and Tullyroan and the urban district of Armagh. 4,191 valid votes; quota 1,048. The first count decided the result."
